  "render_guidance": {
    "grip_center": "hand_socket_px transformed to actor local; never origin+rotating blade_inner",
    "glove": "re-render original texture region at exactly its existing body-aligned location above the grip; do not invent an opaque recolour patch",
    "up_order": "weapon behind body, original body, original glove region",
    "other_order": "original body, weapon, original glove region",
    "hand_pose_transition": "switch socket only when original body atlas row changes; no interpolated floating socket or body bitmap rotation/translation/stretch",
    "walking": "resolve walk row 1/2/3 when these actual body frames are visible; idle socket alone is not accurate for walking",
    "rest": "point tip upward or diagonally upward; do not trail a full-length sword below feet",
    "weapon_form": "code-native compact blade silhouette with dark outline, muted steel body, narrow pale edge and dark hilt; avoid luminous white rod or high-detail photoreal metal",
    "blade_length": "prefer one physically consistent blade length across carried/startup/active/recovery display; final geometry is runtime implementation scope and must share active render/damage endpoints",
    "dead": "weapon may be hidden for dead actor"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "These are existing proxy poses, not newly authored Fin animation or approved Fin handedness.",
    "The visible extended glove is used; down-right/up-left screen placement may read as a left-handed proxy. Fin's approved right sword/left shield identity remains unchanged.",
    "Hand position changes when original row0 changes to row4; right hand moves 28 world pixels forward. Damage distance and first-contact timing must be remeasured without changing approved timing configuration.",
    "Hand/glove interpretation uses original coloured pixels and pose context; independent review and actual direction previews are still required."
